Home-unit closure: the package db exposes q (depends on p) and r (depends
on q).  Loading a unit as a home unit while a db unit that depends on it
stays unloaded must be rejected.  With -hide-all-packages the db units
are invisible, so only genuinely missing home units count.

CHECK-LABEL: == P ==
CHECK:       error: [GHC-03271]
CHECK-NEXT:  Some units are not loaded but depend on loaded units.
CHECK-NEXT:  q-0.1.0.0 -> p-0.1.0.0

CHECK-LABEL: == P Q ==
CHECK:       error: [GHC-03271]
CHECK-NEXT:  Some units are not loaded but depend on loaded units.
CHECK-NEXT:  r-0.1.0.0 -> q-0.1.0.0

CHECK-LABEL: == P R ==
CHECK:       error: [GHC-03271]
CHECK-NEXT:  Some units are not loaded but depend on loaded units.
CHECK-NEXT:  q-0.1.0.0 -> p-0.1.0.0

